WEBVTT

00:00:00.285 --> 00:00:02.619
Suppose you want to test the frontend and

00:00:02.619 --> 00:00:05.352
payment service together using recorded
traffic.

00:00:05.523 --> 00:00:09.114
Start with the two captures and combine
them into one snapshot.

00:00:09.652 --> 00:00:14.654
Record the frontend and payment traffic,
then open the frontend snapshot and append

00:00:14.654 --> 00:00:15.919
the payment snapshot.

00:00:16.090 --> 00:00:18.757
In the guide's example, the merged snapshot

00:00:18.757 --> 00:00:21.735
contains a login the payment requests can
reuse.

00:00:22.285 --> 00:00:27.008
Open Replay from the merged snapshot and
select the test cluster and namespace.

00:00:27.179 --> 00:00:29.566
Make sure both target workloads are running
there.

00:00:30.119 --> 00:00:33.520
In Tests, edit the frontend row and select
its workload.

00:00:33.691 --> 00:00:34.907
Repeat for payment.

00:00:35.078 --> 00:00:37.540
In the routing table, confirm each service

00:00:37.540 --> 00:00:40.412
points to its own deployment before you
continue.

00:00:40.952 --> 00:00:42.354
Select a test config.

00:00:42.525 --> 00:00:46.978
In the review, confirm you have both
inbound traffic sources and check the

00:00:46.978 --> 00:00:49.385
recorded dependencies you chose to mock.

00:00:49.556 --> 00:00:51.034
Then select Start Replay.

00:00:51.585 --> 00:00:53.724
Open the resulting report and check it

00:00:53.724 --> 00:00:56.201
against the two service selections you
made.
